-- CAPABILITY ------------- errors/capture_escape_7.march

`s` cannot leave the `Socket.with_connection` callback, but the `Result` that holds it is returned. [capture_escape]

11 |     let live = Socket.with_connection("example.com", 80, fn s -> Ok(session(s, "ada")))
                                                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

    `s` is a scoped handle: it is only good until the `Socket.with_connection` callback returns (line 11).
    How `s` gets there: line 11: calls `session`.
    Read what you need inside the callback and return the data instead.
    run `march --explain capture_escape`


